Hi John.

> Hi --
> 
> Does anyone know of software for radio path modeling and other topographic 
> work similar to VE2DBE's Radiomobile?  I'd be looking to use it with US DEM 
> data, or possibly the new SRTM data (which I don't really know anything 
> about).

Well, there's SPLAT! (http://www.qsl.net/kd2bd/splat.html), but SPLAT! handles
geometric line-of-sight paths only at the present time.  Depending on what
you're doing, this may be enough.  HOWEVER, there is a group who is in the
process of expanding SPLAT! to follow several different radio propagation
models.  This will probably do what you want (and more).  There are
several others who have expressed interest in doing the same.  I'd like
to get everyone "on the same page", so we can all work together on this.

I created a spot on sourceforge.net to support the project, but I have
not had time to get back to it.  That's (hopefully) about to change.

Last I tried (5 months ago), I was unsuccessful in getting CVS to upload
files to sourceforge.net.  (I've never used CVS to upload files before.)
I'm sure I'm overlooking something simple somewhere...  (Yes, CVS and SSH
are installed, and work fine downloading files.)

So, let's say I have a directory of files on my machine.  How do I get
them from here to there, CVS-wise?

(Apologies for the simple question.)


